  "body": "## Result and scope\n\nThis is an independently replayable **no-defect field-coverage audit**, not a repair, new supplier or new kappa. It adds only `research/selected-generated-identity-audit/`; no frozen source, archive, existing pin or selected record changes.\n\nThe audited comparator is `research/gauge44-slots-t16/code/generated_identity.py`. Inputs are the seven authenticated `slots/local` members of the reviewed PR1042 archive inherited by selected PR1094\u2014not the historical R492 `evidence/local` directory. The exact archive bytes and member hashes stay pinned; the comparator is also bound to the selected-source manifest.\n\n### Exact evidence\n\n- **939,603 retained tree nodes** independently enumerated, including containers, keys, positions and scalar types. The original trees contain 939,604 nodes: only root phase `seconds` is excluded.\n- All **four raw-reference slots** are checked before replacement by content identities.\n- **155 receipt-node omission/replacement mutations**, all rejected. These exhaust both receipt trees except the documented valid-timing replacement; this is not a claim of 939,603 separately executed mutations.\n- **181 total negative controls**, including stale references, Boolean/integer confusion, unfamiliar nested timing fields, invalid timing, lost payload fields with correctly rebound references, serialization drift and truncated gzip.\n- **Nine positive controls**, including controlled gzip recompression and plain-JSON reformatting with updated raw recipe references.\n- Five focused test groups include a deliberately faulty phase projection, exact independent-encoder bytes and immutable archive header drift rejection.\n\nThe expected canonical identities use an independently implemented recursive encoder, not the audited canonicalizer or `json.dumps`. An additional typed-path oracle checks both normalized receipt trees. The two gzip identities bind full decompressed bytes, not a field projection. Generated temporary containers may differ; immutable archive hashes remain strict.\n\n## Reproduction and observed verification\n\nBase: `0b1cccf86e2f5132ed286a26ef0a681a495740ea`. Python 3.12.12, macOS arm64, standard library only.\n\n```sh\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -I -B research/selected-generated-identity-audit/verify.py\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/selected-generated-identity-audit --check-only\nuv run --python 3.12 --no-project python -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/selected-generated-identity-audit\n```\n\nPublication recheck passed in **16.05 seconds combined**:\n\n```text\nPASS_SELECTED_GENERATED_IDENTITY_AUDIT nodes=939603 receipt_mutations=155 positives=9 negatives=181\nPASS_PACKAGE_METADATA_AND_PINS (not a mathematical acceptance check)\nRan 5 tests in 3.892s\nOK\nPASS_REGISTERED_RESEARCH_PACKAGE research/selected-generated-identity-audit outcome=completed\n```\n\n`TASK.json`, `SOURCES.json`, `VERIFY.json`, `RESULT.json` and README retain scope, source/Git-blob pins, explicit replay, deterministic evidence, limitations and an actionable open next question.\n\n## Overlap and attribution\n\nAssigned card: `portable-replay`; coordination: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/discussions/1884.\n\nThe shared offline snapshot covers 543 open PRs (13:23Z) and 529 discussion records (13:25Z), with complete pagination on 2026-10-14. Targeted live checks confirmed these closest PRs remain open at the reviewed heads:\n\n- #1559, `c4f8af1dcf9fc2317c893b6b250007ded5ef879f`: two PR589 gzip byte-comparison sites, not this projection.\n- #1824, `ad5b1248f25a71983b20617e2f3a80be22f03990`: selected final-stage output comparison across interpreters, not this independent complete-tree oracle.\n\nThe existing T37 role-binding audit concerns a different eight-input normalizer. Joint-prefix validation already supplies cross-platform identity agreement; this adds the bounded independent field-coverage and receipt-mutation evidence. The selected1042 lineage-resolution package is credited for locating the actual selected R480 artifacts. Search omits code diffs and most closed-PR bodies, and cached results may miss subsequent work; no novelty guarantee is claimed.\n\nCredit Jeremy Kothe, Rohan Arun, Hao Yan and the retained supplier/compiler lineage; Douglas Colkitt's maintainer replay and identity convention; Maxime Fleury's gzip audit following Antoine Olivier's independent replay. Prepared for Adam Gall with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Apache-2.0; no independent human review claimed.\n\n## Limits and open next question\n\nNo supplier rebuild, selected cold replay, cross-OS run, full caller acceptance audit, execution authentication, universal JSON canonicalization result or full theorem verification. SHA-256 collision resistance and the pinned implementation/input domain remain assumptions. The inherited reader is not claimed to reject all ambiguous JSON merely because this audit's fixture reader does. Production callers may impose additional byte pins beyond the identity function.\n\nA distinct follow-up can audit another overlap-checked normalizer against its explicit role/field contract. This package deliberately makes no broader claim. No merge or selected-frontier change is requested.\n",
